---
id: org.dxos.plugin.readwise
name: ReadwisePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Triages Readwise highlights and notes into Composer. Steve saves articles, PDFs,
and videos to Readwise/Reader and highlights passages with notes; this plugin
pulls those annotations in, proposes a decomposition of each into discrete
comments/questions/to-dos, and lets Steve confirm, edit, or reject each proposal
on a human-gated triage board. Confirmed items land as ordinary `Task`/`Message`
objects, tagged with their intent and linked back to the source document — ready
to use alongside everything else in the workspace.

This is Increment 1 of a larger arc (see `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-04-readwise-annotation-triage-design.md`):
everything lands in Composer; there is no reach into or sync with external work
trackers (Tana, GitHub, Apple Notes). No new ECHO types are introduced — the
plugin composes `Task`, `Message`, `Bookmark`, `AnchoredTo`, `Tag`, `Cursor`,
`Connection`, `AccessToken`, `Kanban`, and `Chat` (all reused as-is from
`@dxos/types`, `@dxos/echo`, `@dxos/plugin-bookmarks`, `@dxos/plugin-connector`,
`@dxos/plugin-kanban`, `@dxos/assistant-toolkit`).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0`         |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`    |

## Types

Wire/domain shapes this plugin introduces (no new ECHO schema types — see above).

```mdl
type Highlight
  desc: One Readwise highlight or synthetic document-note annotation, decoded from the wire response.
  fields:
    readwiseId: string
    text: string          # empty for a synthetic document-note annotation
    note: string
    tags: string[]
    location?: number
    url?: string
    updated: string        # ISO timestamp, the per-item high-water mark
    sourceTitle: string
    sourceAuthor?: string
    sourceUrl?: string
    sourceCategory?: string
    sourceImage?: string
    sourceId: string       # stable per-document id; the Bookmark dedup key
    sourceUniqueUrl?: string
```

```mdl
type IntentKind
  literals: comment | question | todo
```

```mdl
type SuggestedItem
  desc: One AI-proposed candidate item, before Steve confirms/edits/rejects it.
  fields:
    suggestedKind: IntentKind
    text: string           # verbatim source text, never paraphrased
    note?: string
```

```mdl
type Decision
  desc: Steve's confirm/edit/reject decision over one SuggestedItem.
  fields:
    suggestedKind: IntentKind
    finalKind: IntentKind    # may differ from suggestedKind if Steve re-classified it
    text: string
    note?: string
    accept: boolean
```

```mdl
type CaptureResult
  fields:
    created: number
    updated: number
    cards: number
```

## Services

```mdl
service ReadwiseApi
  desc: |
    Authenticated REST client for the Readwise v2 highlights export API,
    reachable via an injectable Transport (direct | vite-proxy | edge-proxy —
    defaulting to the shared EDGE CORS proxy in the browser). Decodes the wire
    response into Highlight, synthesizing one document-note Highlight (empty
    text) per document that has a note but no highlights.
  ops:
    listHighlightsSince(updatedAfter?: string) → ListHighlightsResult
  effects: [http]
  errors:
    ReadwiseError: request failed or returned an unexpected payload
```

## Operations

```mdl
op captureHighlights
  desc: |
    Idempotently captures a batch of Highlight as ECHO objects: one Bookmark
    per distinct source document, one annotation Message per highlight
    (AnchoredTo its Bookmark), and one triage Task card per Message
    (AnchoredTo it, tagged TRIAGE_TAG, status 'todo'). Re-running with the same
    (or a superset of) highlights creates no duplicates; a highlight whose note
    changed updates the existing Message in place.
  input:
    highlights: Highlight[]
  output: CaptureResult
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op ensureTriageBoard
  desc: |
    Finds-or-creates the one tag-scoped triage Kanban per space: a view-variant
    board whose View filters Task by TRIAGE_TAG and pivots on status. Idempotent,
    deduped by a foreign key stamped on the board.
  output: Kanban
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op decomposeAnnotation
  desc: |
    Decomposes a triage card's annotation into candidate items, persisting the
    proposal as the first Message in the card's companion Chat
    (properties.suggestedItems). Idempotent: a second call with an existing
    suggestion message returns the same Chat unchanged without re-running the
    AI call. On model failure, degrades to an empty item list rather than
    failing — a "no suggestions" message is still useful for Steve to confirm/
    edit by hand.
  input:
    card: Task
  output: Chat
  effects: [echo:write, http]
  requires: [AiService]
```

```mdl
op confirmItems
  desc: |
    Materializes Steve's decisions over the AI's suggested items: an accepted
    decision becomes a Message (comment) or a Task (question/todo, status
    'todo'), tagged with its final intent kind, populated with the passage +
    note, AnchoredTo the source Bookmark and linked back to the card. Rejected
    decisions materialize nothing. Records the resolution on the companion-chat
    suggestion message and sets card.status to 'done' — the terminal step of
    the triage flow.
  input:
    card: Task
    decisions: Decision[]
  output:
    results: Obj[]
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op ReadwiseOperation.Sync
  desc: |
    Reconciles Readwise highlights for one SyncBinding: resolves the binding's
    Connection for credentials, pulls every highlight updated since the
    binding's cursor, captures them via captureHighlights, ensures the triage
    board exists, then advances the cursor to the run-start timestamp on
    success (or records the failure on the cursor, leaving the cursor value
    untouched, on failure). Pull-only and idempotent — matches the
    Connector.sync contract so it can be wired as a ConnectorEntry.sync
    operation in a future increment, though Increment 1 triggers it directly
    from the triage board's "Sync Readwise" toolbar action.
  input:
    binding: Ref<SyncBinding>
  output: CaptureResult
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write, http]
```

```mdl
op ReadwiseOperation.Decompose
  desc: |
    UI-facing wrapper around decomposeAnnotation, additionally reading back the
    parsed suggestedItems and the card's own annotation text, so the TriageCard
    surface gets everything it needs in one round-trip.
  input:
    card: Task
  output:
    chat: Chat
    annotationText: string
    items: SuggestedItem[]
  effects: [echo:write, http]
  requires: [AiService]
```

```mdl
op ReadwiseOperation.Confirm
  desc: UI-facing wrapper around confirmItems, invoked by the TriageCard surface's Confirm action.
  input:
    card: Task
    decisions: Decision[]
  output:
    results: Obj[]
  effects: [echo:write]
```

## Components

```mdl
component TriageBoard
  desc: |
    Companion surface for the triage Kanban: three fixed columns (Needs Review
    / In Triage / Done, mapped onto Task.status todo/in-progress/done), each
    populated by re-running the board's View query and filtering client-side.
    The toolbar's "Sync Readwise" action invokes op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync for
    the space's Readwise SyncBinding.
  props:
    kanban: Kanban
    attendableId?: string
  actions:
    sync() → CaptureResult
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ [Sync Readwise]                     │
    ├──────────────┬──────────────┬───────┤
    │ Needs Review │ In Triage    │ Done  │
    │  card        │  card        │ card  │
    │  card        │              │       │
    └──────────────┴──────────────┴───────┘
```

```mdl
component TriageCard
  desc: |
    Article surface for one triage Task card. On mount, runs
    op:ReadwiseOperation.Decompose (idempotent) so a suggestion always exists
    before Confirm is enabled. Renders the annotation (passage + note) and each
    suggested item with accept/reject and edit-kind controls; Confirm
    materializes the accepted decisions via op:ReadwiseOperation.Confirm and
    disables further edits once done.
  props:
    subject: Task
    attendableId: string
  state:
    annotationText?: string
    items?: SuggestedItem[]     # each carrying Steve's editable accept/finalKind decision
    confirmed: boolean
  actions:
    toggleAccept(index: number)
    setFinalKind(index: number, kind: IntentKind)
    confirm() → Obj[]
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ [passage + note]                    │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ ✨ item text          [kind ▾] [✓/✗]│
    │ ✨ item text          [kind ▾] [✓/✗]│
    ├─────────────────────────────────────┤
    │                          [Confirm]  │
    └─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Pull and Capture

  req F-1.1:
    when: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync runs for a binding with a fresh (unset) cursor
    then: every highlight and document-note annotation is captured as a Bookmark + Message pair, and a triage Task card is created in Needs Review for each

  req F-1.2:
    when: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync runs again with an unchanged remote state
    then: no duplicate Bookmarks, Messages, AnchoredTo relations, or triage Tasks are created

  req F-1.3:
    when: a highlight's note changed since the last capture
    then: the existing annotation Message is updated in place rather than a new one being created

  req F-1.4:
    when: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync succeeds
    then: the binding's Cursor advances to the run-start timestamp; on failure the cursor value is left untouched and lastError is recorded
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Credentials

  req F-2.1:
    when: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync resolves credentials for a binding's Connection
    then: the token is read from the Connection's referenced AccessToken
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Triage Board

  req F-3.1:
    when: op:ensureTriageBoard runs in a space with no existing triage board
    then: exactly one Kanban is created, its View filtering Task by TRIAGE_TAG and pivoting on status

  req F-3.2:
    when: op:ensureTriageBoard runs again in the same space
    then: the same Kanban is returned; no second board is created

  req F-3.3:
    when: Steve opens the space
    then: component:TriageBoard renders three columns (Needs Review / In Triage / Done) populated from the triage board's live query
```

```mdl
feat F-4: AI Decomposition

  req F-4.1:
    when: op:decomposeAnnotation runs on a card with no existing suggestion
    then: the AI proposes 0+ candidate items, each tagged comment/question/todo and preserving the source text verbatim, written as the first Message in the card's companion Chat with properties.suggestedItems

  req F-4.2:
    when: op:decomposeAnnotation runs again on the same card
    then: the existing suggestion is returned unchanged; the AI is not called a second time

  req F-4.3:
    when: the AI call fails or returns malformed output
    then: decomposition degrades to an empty item list rather than failing the whole operation
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Confirmation

  req F-5.1:
    when: Steve accepts a suggested item as `comment`
    then: a Message is materialized, tagged `comment`, populated with the passage + note, AnchoredTo the source Bookmark and linked to the card

  req F-5.2:
    when: Steve accepts a suggested item as `question` or `todo`
    then: a Task is materialized with status 'todo', tagged accordingly, populated with the passage + note, AnchoredTo the source Bookmark and linked to the card

  req F-5.3:
    when: Steve rejects a suggested item
    then: no result object is materialized for it

  req F-5.4:
    when: op:confirmItems completes
    then: the resolution (accepted/rejected, final kind, result ref) is recorded on the companion-chat suggestion message, and the card's status is set to 'done'
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Per-Card AI Companion

  req F-6.1:
    when: Steve opens the assistant companion on a triage Task card
    then: the `assistant-chat` companion surface resolves (creating if absent, via EnsureCompanionChat) a persisted Chat scoped to that card
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Sync Action

  req F-7.1:
    when: Steve invokes the triage board's "Sync Readwise" toolbar action
    then: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync is invoked for the space's Readwise SyncBinding

  req F-7.2:
    when: no Readwise SyncBinding exists yet in the space
    then: the sync action is disabled
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Capture is idempotent
  given: a Readwise account with highlights
  when: sync runs, then runs again with no new remote activity
  then:
    - each highlight appears exactly once as a Bookmark + Message pair
    - each annotation has exactly one triage Task card in Needs Review
    - no duplicate Message→Bookmark AnchoredTo relations exist
```

```mdl
test T-2: Note update refreshes in place
  given: a previously-captured highlight whose note has since changed
  when: sync runs again
  then: the existing annotation Message is updated in place; no new Message is created
```

```mdl
test T-3: Credentials resolved from Connection
  given: a Connection referencing an AccessToken
  when: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync resolves credentials
  then: the token yielded matches the AccessToken's token field
```

```mdl
test T-4: Sync captures and advances the cursor
  given: a fresh SyncBinding with an unset cursor
  when: op:ReadwiseOperation.Sync runs, then runs again
  then:
    - the first run creates highlights and exactly one triage board
    - the second run creates no new highlights
    - the cursor value is defined after the first run
```

```mdl
test T-5: Triage board is a singleton per space
  given: a space with no triage board
  when: op:ensureTriageBoard runs twice
  then: exactly one Kanban exists, its View querying Task by TRIAGE_TAG and pivoting on status
```

```mdl
test T-6: AI decomposition persists as the companion chat's first message
  given: a triage card whose annotation contains a question and a to-do
  when: op:decomposeAnnotation runs
  then:
    - the card's companion Chat's first Message carries properties.suggestedItems with a question entry and a todo entry, each preserving the source text
    - the Chat is linked to the card via Chat.CompanionTo
```

```mdl
test T-7: Decomposition is idempotent
  given: a triage card that already has a suggestion message
  when: op:decomposeAnnotation runs again
  then: the same Chat is returned; no second suggestion message is added
```

```mdl
test T-8: Confirmation materializes accepted decisions only
  given: a decomposition with one accepted `question`, one accepted `comment`, and one rejected item
  when: op:confirmItems runs
  then:
    - exactly one Task tagged `question` exists, status 'todo', project unset
    - exactly one Message tagged `comment` exists, containing the passage and note
    - no object tagged `todo` (the rejected item's kind) was created
    - both results are AnchoredTo the source Bookmark and linked to the card
    - the card's status is 'done'
```

```mdl
test T-9: Per-card companion chat resolves
  given: a triage Task card with no companion Chat yet
  when: the assistant-chat companion surface's EnsureCompanionChat runs for that card
  then: a persisted Chat is returned, linked to the card via Chat.CompanionTo
```

```mdl
test T-10: Sync action is registered and resolvable
  given: ReadwisePlugin is active
  when: the operation-handler capability is queried for ReadwiseOperation.Sync
  then: a handler is found — proving the triage board's "Sync Readwise" toolbar action invokes a real, resolvable operation
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: dxos.spec/ext/type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: dxos.spec/ext/feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext test
  uri: dxos.spec/ext/test@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ...
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext service
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0
  desc: An external or system-level dependency providing named operations.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    loading?: eager | lazy
    ops?: OpMap                 # name(params) → ReturnType
    errors?: ErrorMap
    note?: Prose
```
